  "slug": "pangenome-graphs-bd3e",
  "summary": "A draft mouse pangenome graph and a graph-based hominin mtDNA tool show graph references moving into model-organism and ancient DNA analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of graph or circular-aware references in place of a single linear reference. The mouse pangenome paper presents base-level graphs on a C57BL/6J T2T backbone, including founder and CC pangenomes, and reports improved read alignment and variant calling. TrailMix applies a pangenome reference graph to estimate mixture proportions and phylogenetic placement of hominin mtDNA sources in ancient samples. MitoArc addresses a related reference problem for human mtDNA, using shifted-coordinate processing and NUMT evidence in a Nextflow workflow benchmarked on synthetic truth data. The fastpmr preprint is adjacent rather than graph-based: a pairwise mismatch-rate method for relatedness inference, reported over 1000x faster than READv2, applied across the global ancient DNA record.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
